From: yuzu <yuzu23234@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sensors: discard explicitly unreliable gyro and compass reports

Gyroscope startup samples, including full-scale transients, carry
accuracy 0. Rotation vector events also signal unreliable heading with
this status. The measurement signals do not expose accuracy, so do not
forward these samples as usable data.

--- a/src/libssc-sensor-gyroscope.c
+++ b/src/libssc-sensor-gyroscope.c
@@ -85,7 +85,7 @@
 			return;
 		}
 
-		if (msg->n_velocity >= 3) {
+		if (msg->n_velocity >= 3 && msg->accuracy != SSC_ACCURACY_UNRELIABLE) {
 			x = msg->velocity[0];
 			y = msg->velocity[1];
 			z = msg->velocity[2];
--- a/src/libssc-sensor-compass.c
+++ b/src/libssc-sensor-compass.c
@@ -117,7 +117,7 @@
 			return;
 		}
 
-		if (msg->n_rotation >= 4) {
+		if (msg->n_rotation >= 4 && msg->accuracy != SSC_ACCURACY_UNRELIABLE) {
 			x = msg->rotation[0];
 			y = msg->rotation[1];
 			z = msg->rotation[2];
